35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, the pilot floor takes up to nine minutes per person! That’s huge. How does that affect our move timeline?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, the pilot floor delay is separate. My concern is the 6,200 yen per desk fee. Every change costs us.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, the survey data is damning. Daylight was the top complaint, yet the plan gives only four desks windows. We must address this inequity explicitly.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, daylight is irrelevant. The printer row is nine decibels louder. I need the window side, or I’m not moving.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Shion, loud printers are awful! But @Mizuki, daylight matters too. Let’s find a spot where everyone feels comfortable and included, not just one person!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, four desks for five people? That’s unfair! I need to know who gets the window so I can plan my morning routine without stress.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, the billing basis is area, not headcount. We pay for empty space. We must minimize the footprint to stop that monthly drain.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, minimizing footprint ignores the human cost. @Rin, the survey proves daylight is critical. We must assign the window seats deliberately, not by accident.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, minimizing footprint is just another word for maximizing discomfort. I need the quiet zone. The physio note confirms my body needs time to settle.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, minimizing space hurts us! @Shion, I hear you on comfort. Let’s balance quiet spots with daylight so nobody feels left out!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, four window desks means one person gets none. I need to know if that person is me, so I can plan my morning gaps.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, the cost is fixed regardless of who sits where. We pay for the area, not the view.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, the survey shows daylight is the top complaint. We must assign the window seats deliberately, not by accident. Who accepts the interior wall?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
